        <body>
            <div xml:id="d294">

                <pb facs="0458" n="370" sameAs="frus:frus1919Parisv02/pg370"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Robert Lansing Tapers</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        President Wilson
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Paris</hi>
                        </placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1919-01-13">13 January,
                            1919</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. President</hi>: Replying to your letter
                    of the 11th, regarding an interview for King Nicholas of Montenegro, I believe
                    in view of the attitude of the Allied Governments toward the King it would be
                    unwise at the present time to have an interview with him.</p>
                <p>Faithfully yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Robert Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
